{"font":{"id":"fb9ee26c-7a14-476d-b6f3-85e223ba4c15","word":"font","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"source","tags":["feminine"],"word":"fonte"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"1824 — George Gordon, Lord Byron, Don Juan, canto V\nA gaudy taste; for they are little skill'd in\nThe arts of which these lands were once the font","id":"f2fd0246-d0c7-41fd-a772-cc03612f1492"},{"text":"As I am not drawing here on the font of imagination to refresh that of fact and experience, I do not suggest that the Tarot set the example of expressing Secret Doctrine in pictures and that it was followed by Hermetic writers; but it is noticeable that it is perhaps the earliest example of this art.","ref":"1910, Arthur Edward Waite, The Pictorial Key to the Tarot, part II:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[32,36]],"id":"1788c3d4-80d3-44fd-8e00-96dc11ffbfcd"},{"text":"I am interested to fix your attention on this prospect now because unless you take it within your view and permit the full significance of it to command your thought I cannot find the right light in which to set forth the particular matter that lies at the very font of my whole thought as I address you to-day.","ref":"1915, Woodrow Wilson, Third State of the Union Address:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[262,266]],"id":"11338ff0-a8b1-4ad5-b045-e869bf38a284"},{"text":"The Bible lays special stress on the fear of God as the font of wisdom.","ref":"1919, Boris Sidis, The Source and Aim of Human Progress:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[56,60]],"id":"871dcdfd-81f5-4885-b26d-eca81ba323ec"}],"links":[["source","source"],["wellspring","wellspring"],["fount","fount"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations","Quotation templates to be cleaned"],"raw_glosses":["(figuratively) A source, wellspring, fount."],"glosses":["A source, wellspring, fount."],"tags":["figuratively"],"id":"b8f7c1f2-2b3b-4663-9053-954fafe8e6ac"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},